<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The art club at a school in Nyeri draws its logo on a grid. One corner of the logo is <m>L({4},\,{1})</m>, and the logo's area is <m>{12}</m> square units. To make a banner, the logo is first stretched with stretch factor <m>{2}</m> and the x-axis invariant. The result then undergoes the rotation of <m>90^\circ</m> anticlockwise about O.</p><p>(a) Find the single matrix for the two transformations.</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the image of L on the banner.</p><div>( <fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/> , <fillin characters="5" name="ans3"/> )   </div><p>(c) Find the area of the logo on the banner.</p><div><fillin characters="5" name="ans4"/> square units  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The first matrix is <m>A = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]}</m> and the second is <m>B = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -1 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}</m>. The matrix of the transformation done first is written on the right: <m>BA = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -1 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -2 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -2 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{c} 4 \\ 1 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ 4 \end{array}\right]}</m>, so L goes to <m>({-2},\,{4})</m>.</p><p>(c) <m>\det(BA) = {2}</m>, so the area scale factor is <m>{2}</m> and the area on the banner is <m>{2} \times {12} = {24}</m> square units. The stretch multiplies areas by <m>{2}</m>; the second transformation does not change area.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -2 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>4</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>24</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>